/**
 * 📌 GlobalScope – Key Points (Code Editor Notes)
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 1️⃣ What is GlobalScope?
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - GlobalScope is a CoroutineScope provided by Kotlin Coroutines
 * - It is NOT lifecycle-aware
 * - Coroutines launched in GlobalScope live as long as the application process
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 2️⃣ Lifetime of GlobalScope
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - GlobalScope coroutines:
 *     • Do NOT stop when Activity is destroyed
 *     • Do NOT stop on screen rotation
 *     • Do NOT stop when user leaves the screen
 *
 * - They are cancelled only when:
 *     • The app process is killed
 *     • Coroutine is manually cancelled
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 3️⃣ Why GlobalScope is dangerous in Android
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - Can easily cause memory leaks
 * - Holds references to destroyed Activities
 * - Background work may continue with no UI
 * - Can cause crashes when updating UI after Activity is gone
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 4️⃣ Thread behavior
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - GlobalScope.launch { } uses Dispatchers.Default by default
 * - NOT guaranteed to run on Main thread
 * - UI updates must switch to Dispatchers.Main explicitly
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 5️⃣ Example behavior in this Activity
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * Timeline:
 *   1. Activity is created → coroutine starts
 *   2. User exits Activity or rotates screen
 *   3. onDestroy() is called
 *   4. GlobalScope coroutine CONTINUES running
 *   5. "Coroutine Finished after the Delay" still prints
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 6️⃣ Comparison with lifecycleScope
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - lifecycleScope:
 *     • Cancels automatically on onDestroy()
 *     • Safe for UI work
 *
 * - GlobalScope:
 *     • Never cancels automatically
 *     • Unsafe for UI work
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 7️⃣ When GlobalScope should be used (RARE)
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - Very rare cases:
 *     • App-wide background logging
 *     • Analytics fire-and-forget
 *     • Tasks independent of UI
 *
 * - Even in these cases, structured scopes are preferred
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 8️⃣ What NOT to use GlobalScope for
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * ❌ Network calls tied to UI
 * ❌ Database operations for screens
 * ❌ Timers for Activities
 * ❌ Delays related to UI state
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 9️⃣ Better alternatives
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - lifecycleScope → UI-related work
 * - viewModelScope → data that survives rotation
 * - WorkManager → background / long-running tasks
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 🔟 Manual cancellation required
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - If you use GlobalScope, YOU must cancel it manually
 * - Otherwise, coroutine runs until process death
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * 1️⃣1️⃣ Required dependency
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - Comes with Kotlin Coroutines
 * - No lifecycle dependency included
 *
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * ⚠️ Final Warning
 * --------------------------------------------------
 * - GlobalScope is strongly DISCOURAGED in Android UI code
 * - Google officially recommends avoiding it
 * - Use lifecycle-aware scopes instead
 *
 */
